openi2pd notices and third-party attribution

This file summarizes the licenses and provenance of material distributed with
openi2pd. It does not replace the authoritative license texts.

Project code and documentation
------------------------------
The router, libraries, TUI, native tools, packaging, Android application and
project-authored documentation are distributed under BSD-3-Clause. The terms
and copyright holders are recorded in `LICENSE`, `android/LICENSE`,
`docs/LICENSE`, `debian/copyright` and the relevant source provenance records.

Imported tools
--------------
The auxiliary tools in `tools/` are adapted from PurpleI2P/i2pd-tools and are
distributed under the upstream BSD-3-Clause terms in `tools/LICENSE`. The
pinned upstream commit, per-file manifest and divergence record are in
`contrib/upstream/tools-files.txt`, `docs/tools/provenance.md` and repository
history. The upstream text's empty copyright-holder field and clause 3
reference to `i2pd-reseed` are preserved.

Artwork and brand assets
------------------------
The openi2pd name and geometric node/tunnel mark are the project identity. The
canonical vector and raster assets are in `assets/branding/`; the supplied
`logo-original.png` reference is unchanged. Provenance, dimensions and the
original SHA-256 are recorded in `docs/branding/assets.md` and
`assets/branding/colors.md`.

Android dependencies
--------------------
The Android application uses AndroidX and Material Components for Android,
distributed under Apache-2.0. The Gradle wrapper is also distributed under
Apache-2.0. Their notices remain with the resolved artifacts and are not
replaced by this file.

Java reference and interoperability fixtures
--------------------------------------------
The I2P Java implementation is a read-only interoperability reference. It is
not vendored, built, linked or distributed with openi2pd. Fixture provenance
is recorded in `tests/interop/FIXTURES.md`.

Bundled native dependencies
---------------------------
Static and distribution packages may bundle OpenSSL, Boost, zlib, MiniUPnPc,
musl, libstdc++ or platform libraries. Their licenses are recorded in
`contrib/static/debian/copyright-bundled` and in distribution package
metadata. Those terms take precedence over this summary.

Project URLs and the issue tracker are listed in `README.md` and
`docs/index.md`. This file records attribution; it is not a replacement for
the complete license texts.
